Package: npistat
Type: Package
Title: Nonparametric Predictive Inference for Censored and Bernoulli Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("M. Theodor", "Loots", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "theo.loots@gmail.com",
                    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7722-3913"))
Description: Lower and upper probabilities for future observations under Hill's assumption A(n)
    (Hill 1968 <doi:10.1080/01621459.1968.11009286>), expressed through M-functions. For data
    censored on the right, the left or within intervals of arbitrary width, the package gives the
    M-functions of a sharing assumption that reproduces the right-censored theory of Coolen and Yan
    (2004) <doi:10.1016/j.jspi.2003.07.004> exactly, the Turnbull (1976) estimator, and survival
    bounds for the next observation that contain that estimator under every censoring pattern. For
    Bernoulli data it gives bounds on the number of events among several future observations
    (Coolen 1998 <doi:10.1016/S0167-7152(97)00081-3>), and the same bounds from censored data by
    completions. The same C sources back the 'Python' package 'npistat'.
URL: https://github.com/mtloots/npistat
BugReports: https://github.com/mtloots/npistat/issues
License: GPL-3
